From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:25:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] libubox: blobmsg_json: read 64-bit integers without
 assuming alignment

The data of an INT64 blob attribute is only four-byte aligned, and
formatting it as JSON read it with a 64-bit load: undefined behaviour,
which traps on aarch64 in a UBSan build, as in `ubus call` printing a
reply with a 64-bit value.

Add a patch to libubox that reads the value with blobmsg_get_u64(), as
the DOUBLE case does. It is meant for libubox upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/libs/libubox/Makefile                 |  2 +-
 ...-integers-without-assuming-alignment.patch | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/libs/libubox/patches/100-blobmsg_json-read-64-bit-integers-without-assuming-alignment.patch

diff --git a/package/libs/libubox/Makefile b/package/libs/libubox/Makefile
index 5614651..203c844 100644
--- a/package/libs/libubox/Makefile
+++ b/package/libs/libubox/Makefile
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=libubox
-PKG_RELEASE=1
+PKG_RELEASE=2
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL=$(PROJECT_GIT)/project/libubox.git
diff --git a/package/libs/libubox/patches/100-blobmsg_json-read-64-bit-integers-without-assuming-alignment.patch b/package/libs/libubox/patches/100-blobmsg_json-read-64-bit-integers-without-assuming-alignment.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7ae7857
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/libs/libubox/patches/100-blobmsg_json-read-64-bit-integers-without-assuming-alignment.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] blobmsg_json: read 64-bit integers without assuming alignment
+
+Blob attributes are padded to four bytes, so the data of an INT64
+attribute is only four-byte aligned, and blobmsg_format_element() reads
+it with a 64-bit load: undefined behaviour, which traps on aarch64 when
+built with -fsanitize=undefined -fsanitize-trap=undefined, as in
+`ubus call` printing a reply with a 64-bit value.
+
+Read the value with blobmsg_get_u64(), which reads two aligned 32-bit
+words, as the DOUBLE case already does through blobmsg_get_double().
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/blobmsg_json.c
++++ b/blobmsg_json.c
+@@ -269,7 +269,7 @@
+ 		snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), "%" PRId32, (int32_t) be32_to_cpu(*(uint32_t *)data));
+ 		break;
+ 	case BLOBMSG_TYPE_INT64:
+-		snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), "%" PRId64, (int64_t) be64_to_cpu(*(uint64_t *)data));
++		snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), "%" PRId64, (int64_t) blobmsg_get_u64(attr));
+ 		break;
+ 	case BLOBMSG_TYPE_DOUBLE:
+ 		snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), "%.17g", blobmsg_get_double(attr));
